<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Segeju</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Segeju are a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantu-peoples">Bantu-speaking</a> people of the coast on the Kenya–Tanzania border, south of Mombasa. Portuguese and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> sources of the late 16th century describe them as warlike allies of Malindi who helped defeat the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimba">Zimba</a> raiders in 1589 and attacked Mombasa around 1592, clearing the way for the Portuguese and the ruler of Malindi to take over the town.</p></div>
